# 11g's reply to a fetch of 5 rows of `select level ...` (#2466): the row
# header, rows 2 to 6, each but the first behind a bit vector (TTI_BVC), and the
# OER (6 rows so far).
# Captured 2026-11-05 through tools/capture_proxy.py: sqlplus 11.2 (instant
# client 11.2, x86-64 Linux) running statements on Oracle 11g XE 11.2.0.2 with
# SERVER=POOLED, the DRCP pool started. The TTC payload, without the packet's
# header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column and the |ascii| gutter are
# ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
